# Cross-origin isolation, required for SharedArrayBuffer.
#
# The Rust/Wasm audio engine needs SharedArrayBuffer, which the browser only
# exposes to a cross-origin isolated document. vite.config.ts sets these for
# `vite dev` and `vite preview`, and the Electron app sets them itself, but a
# static deployment is served by the host, so the host has to send them.
#
# Without them nothing fails: `crossOriginIsolated` is false, the engine falls
# back to the Web Audio path, and the only symptom is that it sounds different.
#
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this file from the publish directory. Vite
# copies public/ into dist/ verbatim, so it ships with the build.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
